    "date": "2026-08-26",
    "claim": "Theorem 4 gives the exact surface and 17 integral sections; the published height-pairing Gram matrix has determinant 948, proving the sections independent. The paper states rank 17 is maximal over Q(t) for an elliptic K3 surface.",
    "source_model": "y^2 = x^3 - 27*S(t)*x + (27/4)*T(t)",
    "generic_rank_status": "exactly 17 by Elkies: 17 independent sections and the maximal-rank bound for elliptic K3 surfaces over Q(t)",
    "section_reconstruction": "x_1..x_17 and y_1 are printed in full; y_2..y_17 are reconstructed exactly as degree-6 polynomial square roots of the published RHS using the paper's leading-coefficient sign string -+-+++++-+-+++-++.",
    "record_hunt": "v1.3 exposes the exact published MW17 subgroup directly to core Auto Search. Auto Search certifies the 17 specialized sections, searches denominator-1 x on a global minimal integral model while the rigorous lower is below 25, and unlocks general exact affine/rational x charts at rank >=25. The rank-25 threshold is an explicit Rank Hunter search policy, not an attribution of an unpublished historical procedure.",
    "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.25406",
    "doi": "10.48550/arXiv.2608.25406",
    "theorem_reference": "Theorem 4 and §2.2",
    "release_audit_baseline": "36d37730ded550a04ceb383434c466afd81e54c9",
    "release_claim_boundary": "The generic rank-17 theorem is literature provenance for the family. Rank Hunter does not turn it into a specialization lower bound until the 17 specialized sections are exact-certified independent on that fiber."
  },
